slides.content:
# Align Multiple Rows/Columns

`align-content` only works when there are multiple lines (i.e., `flex-wrap: wrap;`). It distributes space between the lines along the cross axis.

Values mirror `justify-content`: `flex-start`, `flex-end`, `center`, `stretch`, `space-between`, `space-around`, `space-evenly`.

```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-content: space-between;
}
```
Without `flex-wrap`, `align-content` has no effect.

slides.codeSnippet:
.gallery {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-content: space-evenly;
  height: 500px;
}
